</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Results</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Evaluation Benchmarks. ‣ 4.1 Experimental Setup ‣ 4 Multilingual Balanced Allocation Performance ‣ Exploring Polyglot Harmony: On Multilingual Data Allocation for Large Language Models Pretraining" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> summarizes the main experimental results, with detailed per-language performance provided in Appendix F. Despite being trained on a relatively modest 1 T-token budget, our 1.2 B-parameter model achieves competitive performance against publicly available models such as LLaMA-3.2, Gemma-3, and Qwen-3. When compared directly to different allocation methods, our <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Climb</span>-derived allocation consistently delivers state-of-the-art results. Notably, we observe absolute performance improvements of up to 2.60% on the XNLI task compared to isolated allocation. On average, <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Climb</span> outperforms the baselines by approximately 1.85% across all evaluated tasks, underscoring the efficacy of our proposed multilingual allocation strategy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S4.F8.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:110.4pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15556v1/7b_res.svg" id="S4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:153/101;" width="153" height="101"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>Different allocation results on 7B model.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="S4.F8.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:110.4pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.15556v1/radar.svg" id="S4.F8.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:107/105;" width="107" height="105"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Illustration of each language allocation methods.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
